2.50 Family Floater Policy means a Policy described as such in the Policy Schedule where the family members (two or more) named in
the Policy Schedule are Insured Persons under this Policy. Only the following family members can be covered under a Family Floater
Policy:
a. Insured Person; and/or
b. Insured Person’s legally married spouse (for as long as she/he continues to be married to the Insured Person); and/or
c. Insured Person’s children who are less than 30 years of Age on the commencement of the Policy Period (a maximum 4 children
can be covered under the Policy as Insured Persons).
